# L1_1 (CuPt-type) ordering target on FCC 4x4x4 = 256 atoms.
# Species: 0 = A, 1 = B; alternating (111) planes of pure A and pure B.
#
# Distinguishing feature: alpha_AB at NN is *zero* because each A in a
# (111) layer has 6 in-plane A + 6 out-of-plane B = balanced. The
# ordering signature appears at 2NN (= the next (111) plane, all
# different species).
#   shell 0 (NN, z=12): P(B|A) = 6/12 = 0.5 = c_B -> alpha_AB = 0
#   shell 1 (2NN, z=6): P(B|A) = 1 (all 2NN are in different (111) plane)
#                        -> alpha_AB = 1 - 1/0.5 = -1
#
# Targeting alpha=0 at NN + alpha=-1 at 2NN is the L1_1 fingerprint;
# the NN target is what keeps SCRAPS from drifting toward L1_0 (which
# would give alpha_AB^NN = -1/3 instead).
SRO 0 1 0 0.0
SRO 0 1 1 -1.0
